  "context_pill": "Section 35AD Asset Transfer",
  "example_summary": "ABC Ltd transfers a building from its specified sugar warehousing unit to a non-specified edible oil unit within the 8-year lock-in period, triggering income recapture.",
  "source_provision": "| Statutory Provision | Core Condition / Trigger | Tax Treatment / Legal Consequence |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Section 35AD(7B)** | Transfer of asset from specified business to non-specified business before 8 years | Deduction allowed less allowable depreciation u/s 32 is deemed as business income |\n| **Section 43(1) Explanation 13** | Subsequent use of asset in non-specified business unit | Actual cost for depreciation is reduced by the depreciation that would have been allowable |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Deemed Income Trap: The difference between the Section 35AD deduction and normal depreciation for the intervening period is brought to tax under PGBP.\n\n\n> [!WARNING] Depreciation Basis: Future depreciation is calculated on the reduced actual cost reflecting notional past depreciation.",
  "director": {
